comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T20:35:34.770Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: searched every status for Ollama embedding batch throughput one-item batches semantic reindex scale vectorization and million-item latency; pm-i25f only proves settings are consumed and no item owns the measured effective-throughput failure caused by equal per-item and per-request ceilings."
  "2026-09-25T14:31:28.375Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: the rich-input regression failed on the existing implementation (request sizes 1,2 instead of 3). The revised scheduler separates the per-input corpus ceiling from a bounded JSON request-byte ceiling, preserves ordering and duplicate positions, splits HTTP 413 or timeout failures, and exposes actual request/retry/split throughput receipts. Real loopback HTTP integration tests pass for 32 rich inputs, Unicode/escaping budgets, payload-too-large recovery and pre-dispatch refusal. Full acceptance and shipping verification remain pending."
  "2026-09-25T14:39:17.096Z","harness:codex","Real-provider acceptance: local Ollama qwen3-embedding:0.6b embedded 32 synthetic rich inputs (each truncated to the existing 3,200-character corpus ceiling) into 32 ordered 1,024-dimensional vectors in one successful HTTP request. Receipt: planned_batches=1, requests=1, split_batches=0, retries=0, elapsed_ms=3103, inputs_per_second=10.31. This proves effective rich-input batching on the actual model; it is not a million-item throughput extrapolation."
  "2026-09-25T14:58:50.792Z","harness:codex","Delivery is recorded by Changeset pm-g0b88h. The rich-input collapse is repaired and real-provider acceptance passes. Keep this canonical issue open for tokenizer-aware budgets, parallel/resume recovery, ETA and declared 100k/1M throughput/memory acceptance; those outcomes are not claimed by this PR."
  "2026-09-25T15:04:16.040Z","harness:codex","Public-package boundary check caught a documentation/export mistake before review: runtime-primitives is an internal SDK barrel, not an exported package subpath. The batching function and its types are now exposed from the existing public sdk/query entrypoint, and the real HTTP integration test imports that barrel. The changelog omission is separately tracked and fixed in pm-changelog as pmc-k1oq."
